        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Table of Contents - Page 34</title>\n  <script>\n    window.MathJax = {\n      tex: {\n        inlineMath: [['$', '$']],\n        displayMath: [['$$', '$$']],\n        processEscapes: true\n      }\n    };\n  </script>\n  <script async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n  <style>\n    * {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n\n    html,\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n      background: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    body {\n      color: #000000;\n      font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    }\n\n    .page {\n      position: relative;\n      width: 1700px;\n      min-height: 2200px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n      padding: 49px 49px 0;\n      background: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .toc-link {\n      margin: 0;\n      color: #0000cc;\n      font-size: 28px;\n      font-weight: normal;\n      line-height: 1.1;\n    }\n\n    .content {\n      margin-top: 68px;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 1.16;\n    }\n\n    .content p {\n      margin: 0 0 35px;\n      text-align: left;\n    }\n\n    .content p.indented {\n      text-indent: 55px;\n    }\n\n    sup {\n      position: relative;\n      top: -0.1em;\n      font-size: 67%;\n      line-height: 0;\n    }\n\n    .peer-tables {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 568px 568px;\n      column-gap: 14px;\n      width: 1150px;\n      margin: 41px auto 0;\n    }\n\n    table {\n      width: 100%;\n      border-collapse: collapse;\n      table-layout: fixed;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 1.12;\n    }\n\n    col.company {\n      width: 438px;\n    }\n\n    col.flag {\n      width: 43px;\n    }\n\n    th,\n    td {\n      padding: 0;\n      vertical-align: top;\n      font-weight: normal;\n    }\n\n    thead th {\n      border-bottom: 2px solid #000000;\n      font-size: 21px;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      line-height: 1.05;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    thead th.company-heading {\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    tbody td.company-name {\n      padding-right: 8px;\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n\n    tbody td.flag {\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    tbody tr.standard {\n      height: 31px;\n    }\n\n    tbody tr.double {\n      height: 62px;\n    }\n\n    tbody tr.spacer {\n      height: 31px;\n    }\n\n    .continuation {\n      display: block;\n      padding-left: 29px;\n    }\n\n    .page-number {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 1617px;\n      left: 0;\n      width: 100%;\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 1;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    .bottom-rule {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 1699px;\n      left: 49px;\n      width: 1604px;\n      height: 6px;\n      background: #858585;\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 1700px) {\n      .page {\n        transform-origin: top left;\n      }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <h1 class=\"toc-link\">Table of Contents</h1>\n\n    <section class=\"content\">\n      <p>Committee's own judgment of the results achieved by our CEO as compared to goals established at the beginning of the fiscal year.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"indented\">As mentioned above, the Compensation Committee reviews relevant market and industry practices on compensation packages to monitor the market practices for compensating our desired talent pool, including data from our Peer Companies (as described below) for the three major components of our compensation program. The Compensation Committee, however, does not set compensation components to meet specific benchmarks, such as targeting salaries \"at the 50 <sup>th</sup> percentile\" or equity compensation \"at the 75 <sup>th</sup> percentile\". Rather, the Compensation Committee reviewed this peer data as a reference point in determining whether each executive's compensation level properly reflects the executive's role and scope of responsibilities relative to our peers and companies with whom we compete for talent.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"indented\">For fiscal year 2010, our human resources department obtained the full Radford Executive Survey of 149 companies, or the Radford Companies. From the list of Radford Companies, Hewitt and our human resources department recommended and our Compensation Committee approved, with only minor changes from the recommendations, three different groups of Peer Companies: employee peers, executive peers and semiconductor peers. Employee peers are the companies in various industries with which we feel we generally compete for talent. Executive peers are a subset of the employee peer list that (i) had revenue levels of &#36;500 million to &#36;5 billion, and thus were similar in size to our anticipated revenue levels for fiscal year 2010, and (ii) had an established business and market presence and, thus, were similar in complexity. Semiconductor peers are all the companies in the semiconductor industry from the Radford Executive Survey. For fiscal year 2010, our employee peers (listed under the column titled \"EE\" below), executive peers (listed under the column titled \"EX\" below) and semiconductor peers (listed under the column titled \"SC\" below) consisted of the companies listed below, or our Peer Companies.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"peer-tables\" aria-label=\"Peer Companies\">\n      <table>\n        <colgroup>\n          <col class=\"company\">\n          <col class=\"flag\">\n          <col class=\"flag\">\n          <col class=\"flag\">\n        </colgroup>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th class=\"company-heading\">Company Name</th>\n            <th>EE</th>\n            <th>EX</th>\n            <th>SC</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Adobe Systems, Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Agilent Technologies, Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Altera Corporation</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Amazon.Com, Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Apple Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Autodesk, Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Avago Technologies Limited</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Broadcom Corporation</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Cadence Design Systems, Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Cisco Systems, Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"spacer\"><td colspan=\"4\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Cypress Semiconductor Corporation</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Dell Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"spacer\"><td colspan=\"4\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Ebay Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"spacer\"><td colspan=\"4\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Electronic Arts Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">EMC Corporation</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Ericsson Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Google Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Infineon Technologies AG</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Intel Corporation</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Intuit Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">Juniper Networks, Inc.</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n          <tr class=\"standard\"><td class=\"company-name\">KLA-Tencor Corporation</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\">X</td><td class=\"flag\"></td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <table>\n        <colgroup>\n          <col class=\"compa